# A `super` in a block handed to `define_method` or
# `define_singleton_method` sent by name is the defined method's: it says
# nothing of an override by the method around it, which kept that method
# off `test-only` as one an unindexed ancestor's caller may run. Sibling of
# 666's nested `def`.
dead lib Widget#install=test-only!~super Widget#direct=test-only!~super Widget#run=unreferenced~super
